[#:seon.task{:name "a-deleted-functions-fault-never-resolves"
             :plan "resolution needs the fault's function entity, so a fault naming a deleted function can never resolve: the seon.flow/release-admission! ClassCastException fault stays open after 69229772b deleted the function and its cause. Also faults whose operation never had a function entity: superv.async/throw-if-exception- (477a97dc, 67029fe7, 2026-09-27) can resolve only by resolve!. The wider rule is task seon.error/health-stays-faulted-on-dead-process-faults. Read `seon.error/resolution`, `docs/research/agent-platform/landing/inv-lifecycle-storage-opus-2026-09-26.md`, `docs/research/agent-platform/stability-sweep-2026-09-27.md` and `docs/seon/issues/a-fault-whose-function-is-deleted-never-resolves.md`."}
