 #:seon.task{:name "fault-window-derives-the-error-selector-when-no-error-occurred"
             :plan "`seon.error/occurred-since` computes observation-selector whenever its query answers a vector, even an empty one; the selector is held per projection, so the first pass after any declaration write rederives it over the whole registry: 12-13 MB and 13.5 ms of the 94 MB pass after a defn (defn-why, 2026-10-08). Derive the selector only when the window holds an error, and hold it by the schema forms it reads (as `seon.program/program-attributes` now is), not by the projection value. Done when the pass after a defn allocates nothing in observation-selector with no errors in its window. Read `seon.error/observation-selector` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/defn-why/defn-why.md`."}
