             :plan "Error notifications to root are outside messages whose text is a pr-str of the error map (a second printer), delivered through :seon.config.error/escalate-to. Done when the notification carries the error's identity (signature, task, handle) as data and no printed copy. Read `seon.error/commit-call`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-guessed-schema-key-is-answered-with-the-nearest-registered-schemas"
             :plan "A schema key an agent guesses (`(malli.core/validate :inst x)`, `:seon.render.transcript/instant`) fails with Malli's `:malli.core/invalid-schema` and `seon.error/reply-value` answers only that bare message, so agent parity-duration-1 (default c53c9306e) spent its fifteen calls hunting a schema for an instant and never wrote a contract; the registry's instant schema is the predicate `inst?`, a symbol key, which its `(filter keyword?)` listings also missed. Like `seon.error/nearest-names` for a guessed symbol, the reply names the registered schemas nearest the guessed key under `:seon.error/nearest`. Asserted by `seon.error-test/a-guessed-schema-key-is-answered-with-the-nearest-registered-schemas`. Red on HEAD ec51e6780: `(seon.error/reply-value database error)` for the `:malli.core/invalid-schema` cause of `(malli.core/validate :inst x)` returns no `:seon.error/nearest`, because `seon.error/missing-symbol` reads only `:sci.impl/symbol` and `:seon.program/not-found` and finds nothing in this cause, so no name is looked up. Correct at the producer: the guessed key is the `:malli.core/invalid-schema` cause's `:schema` in its ex-data; `missing-symbol`'s reader (or a sibling for schema keys) names it, and `nearest-names` ranks the registered schemas by it (the registry's `inst?` symbol key included). Read `malli.core/validate` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/parity-probe.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "prepare-preserves-the-installed-instrumentation-arm-variant"
             :plan "`seon.error/prepare` must return a value admitted by `:seon.error/prepared` when an instrumentation observation carries `:seon.instrument/arm :guard`. Lane sol-retire-connection's edit-hook SCI entrance on default 2b49056a8 repeatedly refuses the recording itself: expected :input or :output, got :guard, called by `seon.error/recording`. Make the producer and its installed error schema agree so the original error is recorded and delivered. Read `malli.core/-instrument`, `seon.instrument/violation`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/sol-loose-ends.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/sol-retire-connection.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-blank-error-message-is-replaced-by-the-sentence-that-describes-the-source"
             :plan "`seon.error/message` answers a message that is not blank for every source: a map whose `:seon.error/message` is whitespace-only is read as having no message (it returns \"   \" unchanged today, against its docstring \"Never absent, never blank\"), so the transition sentence, the root cause's message or the unclassified sentence answers instead. Read `seon.error/message` and `:seon.error/message`."
             :seon.task/children #{[:seon.task/sym seon.error/prove-a-blank-error-message-is-replaced]
                                   [:seon.task/sym seon.error/implement-a-blank-error-message-is-replaced]}}
 #:seon.task{:name "prove-a-blank-error-message-is-replaced"
             :step :prove
             :product #{seon.error-test/a-blank-error-message-is-replaced-by-the-sentence-that-describes-the-source}
             :instructions "In `seon.error-test` add a table test of `seon.error/message` inputs to the messages they answer, including a whitespace-only message case (source `{:seon.error/message \"   \"}`, failure nil) and an empty-string case, asserting each answer is a non-blank string and a non-blank message is returned unchanged. Tag it `^{:seon/tasks #{'seon.error/implement-a-blank-error-message-is-replaced}}`. `seon.error/message` is private: call it through its Var, `(#'seon.error/message source failure)`. Run it red on your branch."}
 #:seon.task{:name "implement-a-blank-error-message-is-replaced"
             :step :implement
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.error/prove-a-blank-error-message-is-replaced]}
